## Synopsis
COMP1002 Final Assignment:
ZipRide Dispatch System

## Contents
README - readme file for COMP1002 Final Assignment
stack_queue.py - contains source code for Stack and Queue
linked_list.py - contains source code for linked list. Used in DSAHashTable for chaining
graph.py - contains source code for Graph
hash_table.py - contains source code for Hash Table
min_heap.py - used to create priority queue which was used to write code to implement dijkstra
max_heap.py - contains source code for Heap (used to store passenger pickup requests based on highest priority
advanced_sorting.py - contains source code for Sorting algorithms (Bubble Sort, Top down Merge Sort and Median of Three Quick Sort)
conditions_module4.py - contains class with modules which return a copy of list input whose contents have been shuffled, another which
                        displaces 10% of contents of input list copy(nearly sort)
                        and reverses input list copy


test_module1.py - contains test code for module 1

test_module2.py - Demonstrate successful searches, deletions and insertions. Provides log of performance
                  Demonstrates collision and load factor at every 10 insertions
test_module2.csv - hash table with output from test_module2.py

test_module3.py - contains test code for module 3

test_module4.py - contains test code for module 4
2000Pickup(module4).csv - contains 2000 passenger records used inside test_module4.py
module4_driver_records.csv - contains 2000 driver records used inside test_module4.py

passenger_driver_records.csv - stores 45 records of both passengers and drivers
records_output.csv - stores the passenger and driver records after they are added to hash table

passengers.csv - contains normal records for passengers
drivers.csv - contains normal records for drivers
passenger_hash_table.csv - contains passenger records after hashing (used in module 3: Heap)
driver_hash_table.csv - contains driver records after hashing   (used in module 3: Heap)


graph.png - snapshot of graph (all locations and roads with driving time)

main.py - main code for ZipRide Dispatch System program
## Dependencies
networkx - used only for graph visualisation
csv - used to read from and write into csv files

Run python3 test_module1.py to test module 1
Run python3 test_module2.py to test module 2
Run python3 test_module3.py to test module 3
Run python3 test_module4.py to test module 4
Run python3 main.py which uses all modules
